  "index": 4,
  "response": "The text is a speech given by Pope Urban II in 1095 to a council of nobles and soldiers, urging them to embark on a crusade to reclaim the Holy Land from Muslim control. The pope emphasizes the importance of the city of Jerusalem, which he refers to as the \"navel of the world,\" and the need to liberate it from the enemies of God. He highlights the glory and greatness of previous Christian monarchs who have destroyed pagan kingdoms and extended the territory of the Holy Church. The pope exhorts the soldiers to recall the valor of their ancestors and to undertake this journey for the remission of their sins, with the promise of imperishable glory in the kingdom of heaven.",
